title: Dead Beacon
tags: [prior, mystery, discovery]
context: journey
weight: 6
cooldown: 8
---

=== intro

The sensors ping something massive—a structure, drifting in the void. As you approach, the shape becomes clear: a Beacon station. One of the Prior network nodes that went dark during the Silence.

It's huge. Kilometers across. Dark, but not quite dead—there's a faint energy signature deep inside. After three centuries, something still hums.

* [Investigate the energy signature]
  ~ fuel -= 5
  -> interior

* [Keep your distance—Beacons are dangerous]
  ~ chronicle "Beacon Sighted"
    Passed a dead Beacon station. Three centuries dark, but not quite dead. We didn't investigate. Some mysteries kill.
  -> END

=== interior

The docking bay still functions, somehow. Inside, the Beacon is cathedral-vast and utterly silent. Prior architecture—curves and angles that don't quite make sense, surfaces that seem to shift when you're not looking directly at them.

The energy signature comes from a chamber deep within. On a pedestal, a shard of something crystalline pulses with faint light.

* [Take the shard]
  ~ addCard relic_beacon_shard
  ~ flag took_beacon_shard
  ~ chronicle "Beacon Shard"
    Took a fragment from a dead Beacon. The Science Collective would pay anything for this. That's not why we're keeping it.
  -> END

* [Leave it—this place feels wrong]
  ~ morale -= 5
  ~ chronicle "Beacon Retreat"
    Left the Beacon empty-handed. The crew breathed easier once we were away. Some treasures aren't worth the taking.
  -> END
